{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:27.053Z","data":{"turn":37,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Very interesting. The login endpoint is using the general `apiLimiter` (1000 requests per 15 minutes in development) and not the `authLimiter` (20 per 15 minutes). This is a significant finding.\\n\\nAlso, I can see:\\n- Strict-Transport-Security is present in the response headers, but this is served over plain HTTP (not HTTPS) - so HSTS is being sent over HTTP which is meaningless since there's no HTTPS endpoint. The HSTS header on an HTTP-only server provides no protection.\\n- RateLimit-Policy: 1000;w=900 - this is the general API limiter, not the auth-specific one with 20 requests\\n\\n\\n- Now I need to verify whether the authLimiter is actually being applied to the login, register, and forgot-password endpoints, or if they're all incorrectly using the general limiter.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:27.053Z"}}
