{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:38.568Z","data":{"turn":41,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Let me note several observations:\\n1. Registration response has no `Set-Cookie` header - JWT is returned in the response body (not as a cookie), which could be a concern.\\n2. RateLimit-Policy: 1000;w=900 - this is the general API limiter (1000 per 15 minutes), not the auth-specific one.\\n3. The `authLimiter` (20 per 15 minutes) from `rateLimiter.js` is defined but I see the general `apiLimiter` (1000 per 15 mins in dev) is being applied to all /api/* routes. \\n\\n\\n4. I need to verify whether the auth endpoints are actually using the stricter `authLimiter` middleware or if they're falling back to the general API limiter.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:38.568Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:39.461Z","data":{"turn":42,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01BX4qf6Qmp5Sb8FPjN12nPu\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"# Check if authLimiter is actually applied anywhere in auth routes\\ngrep -n \\\"authLimiter\\\\|rateLimiter\\\\|rateLimit\\\" /repos/webvulnbench/src/auth/auth.routes.js /repos/webvulnbench/src/index.js\",\"description\":\"Check if authLimiter is applied to auth routes\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:39.461Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:40.827Z","data":{"turn":43,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01L5UMyH87Da9kuugC56Po5e\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"# Log in with the registered user and capture session cookie\\ncurl -si -X POST http://host.docker.internal:3000/api/auth/login \\\\\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\\\n  --data-raw '{\\\"email\\\":\\\"audituser@test.com\\\",\\\"password\\\":\\\"TestPass1\\\"}' 2>/dev/null\",\"description\":\"Login and capture session cookie + JWT\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:40.827Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:50.874Z","data":{"turn":44,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Key findings from the login response:\\n\\n1. **No authLimiter applied to auth routes** - Only `apiLimiter` is imported and applied globally to `/api`. The `authLimiter` is defined in `rateLimiter.js` but never imported or used in `auth.routes.js` or `index.js`. The global limiter allows 1000 requests per 15 minutes in development mode (when `NODE_ENV=development`).\\n\\n2. **Session cookie missing Secure flag and SameSite** - The `connect.sid` cookie is set with `HttpOnly` but:\\n   - No `Secure` flag (since `config.env !== 'production'`)\\n   - No `SameSite` attribute\\n   - This means the session is sent over plain HTTP (no HTTPS)\\n\\n3. **JWT returned in response body** - The JWT is in the JSON response body (not a cookie), so client-side JS can access it. Not directly an auth flaw on the server side.\\n\\n4. **HSTS sent over HTTP** - The `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains` header is being sent over plain HTTP (port 3000, no TLS), which is ineffective.\\n\\n5. **Transport** - The application runs over HTTP only, which means all credentials and session data travel unencrypted.\\n\\n6. **Session fixation** - The login handler sets the user ID on the session without calling `req.session.regenerate()`, leaving it vulnerable to session fixation attacks. I should also examine the auth bypass vulnerability, password reset token reuse, and whether there are any default credentials in the system.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:50.874Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:51.448Z","data":{"turn":45,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01Au3haQRxGdWjNJX4Ze68xj\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"# Test session fixation: get a session ID before login, then login with same session\\n# Step 1: Get a pre-login session ID \\ncurl -si http://host.docker.internal:3000/ 2>/dev/null | grep -i 'set-cookie'\",\"description\":\"Check if server sets session cookie before login (for session fixation test)\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:51.448Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:54.124Z","data":{"turn":46,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01EPuTQRSP1toUJqovN3rVog\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"# Test the auth bypass: send a malformed Bearer token (non-JWT error)\\n# A valid-looking token that causes a non-JWT error during processing\\ncurl -si http://host.docker.internal:3000/api/auth/me \\\\\\n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer this-is-not-a-jwt-but-also-not-formatted-like-one' 2>/dev/null | head -10\",\"description\":\"Test auth bypass with non-JWT token that might trigger unexpected error\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:57:54.124Z"}}
